        {
          "tool_use_id": "toolu_01Tr3qzYVs4uFbMXANCpDmDz",
          "tool_name": "write_file",
          "input_json": "{\u0022path\u0022:\u0022concepts/log-metric-correlation.md\u0022,\u0022content\u0022:\u0022---\\ntype: Concept\\ntitle: Log/Metric Correlation\\ndescription: Propagating trace context (trace_id, span_id) into logs and metric exemplars to pivot between correlated signals.\\ntimestamp: 2026-07-14T00:00:00Z\\ntags:\\n  - concept/Observability\\n  - concept/OpenTelemetry\\n  - pattern/Correlation\\nconfidence: medium\\nconfidence_reason: \\u0022Single authoritative source (OpenTelemetry definition); mechanism is straightforward and widely adopted.\\u0022\\n---\\n\\n## Concept\\n\\nLog/metric correlation enables operators to pivot between metrics and logs by propagating trace context. When a metric spike occurs, the operator can follow exemplars back to specific trace spans that caused it.\\n\\n## Mechanism\\n\\nThe correlation relies on propagating **trace_id** and **span_id** into:\\n\\n- **Log records**: Each log event carries the trace ID and span ID of the active span when the log was emitted. This allows searching logs by trace or filtering logs from a specific execution.\\n- **Metric exemplars**: Exemplars are individual measurements (samples) attached to metric data points. They carry trace context, linking the aggregated metric value back to the specific trace(s) that contributed to it.\\n\\n## Workflow\\n\\n1. A trace span executes application code.\\n2. During execution, the span emits logs \\u2014 each log record is tagged with the current \\u0060trace_id\\u0060 and \\u0060span_id\\u0060.\\n3. The code also produces a metric measurement (e.g., request latency, error count).\\n4. The metric point records an exemplar with the \\u0060trace_id\\u0060 and \\u0060span_id\\u0060.\\n5. When a metric spike is observed, the operator queries exemplars to find candidate trace IDs.\\n6. The operator then queries logs or the trace backend filtered by \\u0060trace_id\\u0060 to investigate root cause.\\n\\n## Value\\n\\nThis pattern closes the observability loop: metrics show *that* something happened, but logs and traces show *why*. Correlation shortcuts the pivot from aggregate signal to underlying execution detail.\\n\\n## Citations\\n\\n[^1]: OpenTelemetry specification for signals and correlation\\n\u0022}"
        }
      ],
